## Summary
A research team at Sahmyook University, led by Professor Lee Yong-woo, has scientifically demonstrated the effectiveness of virtual reality (VR) technology in physical therapy education. This study provides empirical evidence that VR-based training can enhance learning outcomes in rehabilitation contexts.

## Key Points
- Scientific proof of VR's effect in improving physical therapy education.
- Research conducted by a team at Sahmyook University.
- Potential for VR technology to enhance medical training and rehabilitation practices.
- Evidence-based validation supporting technology integration in healthcare education.


